# NexMesh Framework Rules

## Project Structure
- Features/ folder per business module (vertical slices)
- One entity + one API file per feature
- Program.cs: explicit registration, one line per package

## Entity Pattern
```csharp
// Inherit only what you need
public class Order : ISoftDelete, IAudited, IHasConcurrencyStamp, ITenantEntity
{
    public Guid Id { get; set; }  // or long for snowflake ID
    // ISoftDelete
    public bool IsDeleted { get; set; }
    // IAudited (auto-filled)
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
    public string? CreatedBy { get; set; }
    public DateTime? UpdatedAt { get; set; }
    public string? UpdatedBy { get; set; }
    // IHasConcurrencyStamp (optimistic concurrency)
    public string ConcurrencyStamp { get; set; } = "";
    // ITenantEntity
    public string? TenantId { get; set; }
}
```

## API Pattern (AutoApi - recommended)
```csharp
public interface IOrderApi : IAutoApi
{
    [HttpGet("{id}")] Task<OrderDto?> FindAsync(long id);
    [HttpPost] Task<OrderDto> CreateAsync(CreateOrderRequest req);
}
public class OrderApi(IRepository<Order> repo) : IOrderApi { ... }
// Program.cs: builder.Services.AddNexMeshAutoApi(); app.MapNexMeshAutoApi();
```

## Error Handling
```csharp
throw new MeshException("message", errorCode: 40401, statusCode: 404);
// Framework converts to unified JSON automatically. No try-catch needed.
```

## Pagination (mandatory)
```csharp
var page = await db.Get().Select<Order>()
    .OrderByWhitelist(sortBy, whitelist: ["CreatedAt", "Amount"])
    .ToPagedResultAsync(pageIndex, pageSize);
// Returns: Items + TotalCount + PageIndex + PageSize + TotalPages
```

## Caching
```csharp
// Read: cache-first with single-flight
var result = await cache.Get().GetOrCreateAsync(key, TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5), factory, ct);
// Write: always invalidate after update
await cache.Get().RemoveAsync(key);
```

## Error Codes
- 400xx: validation, 401xx: auth, 404xx: not found
- 40901: duplicate submit, 40902: concurrency conflict
- 429: rate limited, 500: internal

## Rules
- DTOs are records, never expose entity internals
- Sorting must use whitelist (no raw user input)
- Events published after transaction commit
- Secrets from environment variables only
- Zero build warnings required
